{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"title":"Anatomy of a Game","role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"],["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapDiagnostics"],["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMapAndExits"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/anatomyofagame"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Gnusto game is one type conforming to "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". That one type carries everything: the rooms and things, where they start, and the rules that govern them. This article is the model underneath — how the engine finds your declarations, how one value is both a declaration and a live reference, and how the world that never changes is kept apart from the state that does."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Declarations are stored properties","anchor":"Declarations-are-stored-properties","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rooms, things, and custom state are declared as "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"stored properties"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" of the game type:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct OperaHouse: Game {","    let foyer = Location { name(\"Foyer of the Opera House\") }","    let bar   = Location { name(\"Foyer Bar\"); dark }","    let cloak = Item { name(\"velvet cloak\"); wearable }","    @Global var disturbances = 0","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you construct the world with "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld\/init(game:saveDirectory:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", the engine’s bootstrap reflects over the game value with "},{"code":"Mirror","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and collects every "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". It names each entity after the property it was stored in: "},{"code":"foyer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"\"foyer\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"cloak","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes "},{"code":"\"cloak\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and so on. You never write these IDs by hand — the property name "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"is"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the name."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is why declarations must live in the type’s main body, not an extension: Swift only allows stored properties there, and the Mirror only sees stored properties. (When even the declarations need to span files or ship separately, that is what a "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" bundle is for — see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":".)"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"One value, two roles","anchor":"One-value-two-roles","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A declaration and a live reference are the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"same value"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let cloak = Item { name(\"velvet cloak\"); wearable }   \/\/ the declaration","","\/\/ …later, inside a rule body:","cloak.after(.take) {","    if cloak.isWorn { … }        \/\/ the live reference — reads current state","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"cloak","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Written in the game body it "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"declares"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the cloak. Used in a rule it "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"reads and writes the live cloak’s state"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isWorn","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isHeld","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/name","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and so on all consult the current turn."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This works because each "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" mints a private identity token when it is created. The token — not the struct’s contents — is the entity’s identity, and it survives copying. Two items are equal when they share a token ("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/==(_:_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"). Inside a turn, the token resolves to the entity’s "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and then to its state; outside a turn there is no state to read, so a live property access traps with an explanation rather than returning a meaningless value."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"References are always compile-checked. "},{"code":"cloak.after(.take)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"hook.holds(cloak)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"foyer.north(bar)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — every one is ordinary property access, so renaming a room or deleting an item breaks the build instead of the running game."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Scenery","anchor":"Scenery","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every noun a room description names should answer when the player examines it. Declare a fixture with "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/scenery(_:adjectives:synonyms:description:_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let wall = Item.scenery(","    \"stone wall\", adjectives: \"rough\", synonyms: \"masonry\", \"old brickwork\",","    description: \"Mortar fills the cracks.\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This creates an ordinary "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" with a name, vocabulary, examine text, and the "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/scenery","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" trait. The fixture cannot be taken and gets no stock room-listing sentence. The name and synonyms contribute nouns and adjectives through the usual parser rules: "},{"code":"stone wall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" answers to "},{"code":"wall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"stone wall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"old brickwork","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" adds "},{"code":"brickwork","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the adjective "},{"code":"old","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"adjectives:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"synonyms:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are variadic, so they read the way "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/synonyms(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" read inside an "},{"code":"Item { }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block — one phrase per argument, no brackets. A synonym is a noun phrase, not a single word, which is why "},{"code":"old brickwork","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" above counts as one argument."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Store it on your game or content bundle and place it in "},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", just like any other item:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var map: WorldMap {","    player.starts(in: hall)","    wall.starts(in: hall)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All arguments after the name are optional. Use the trailing trait block when scenery has another role:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let niche = Item.scenery(\"shadowed niche\", synonyms: \"alcove\") {","    container","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The niche can hold things and take item rules. For text that turns on the niche’s own state — open or shut, lit or dark — omit "},{"code":"description:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and put "},{"code":"description(when: \\.isOpen, …, otherwise: …)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in the trait block; for text that depends on anything else, attach a "},{"code":"niche.describe { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" rule. Without any description, examining it uses the game’s stock examine line. Placement determines where a piece of scenery is visible, just as it does for other items."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The parts of the `Game` protocol","anchor":"The-parts-of-the-Game-protocol","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" gathers a handful of members, most with defaults so a small game declares only what it needs:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"intro","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"tagline","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"maxScore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the banner and scoring metadata."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — geography and initial placement, as a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Read once at startup to build the initial state."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — all game logic, as a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" value. Defaults to empty."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — player-typeable verbs this game adds, as "},{"code":"[SyntaxRule]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Defaults to empty. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — content bundles the game composes itself from, as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Defaults to empty. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The protocol extension also hands every game three ambient references usable as bare identifiers inside "},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" blocks:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"player","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", for its location, score, and inventory, and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player\/item","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the player as a thing in the world (what "},{"code":"X ME","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" examines)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"world","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/World","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", for rules that apply everywhere (like daemons)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"command","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Command","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" currently being performed, inside a rule body."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"The `map` block","anchor":"The-map-block","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a result-builder property that yields a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — a flat list of "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/MapEntry","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" statements: exits, initial item placements, and the player’s start."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var map: WorldMap {","    foyer.south(bar)                 \/\/ an exit","    bar.north(foyer)                 \/\/ and the way back, stated separately","","    player.starts(in: foyer)         \/\/ where the player begins","    cloak.startsWorn                 \/\/ where each thing begins","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exits are one-way, so an asymmetric map needs no special case. There are five kinds of exit and eight ways to place a thing; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMapAndExits","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" covers all of them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Immutable definition, mutable state","anchor":"Immutable-definition-mutable-state","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Internally, the engine keeps two things strictly apart:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"definition"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is everything that never changes during play: names, descriptions, exits, rules, and the parser’s vocabulary. It is built once, from your declarations, at startup."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is everything that "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"does"}]},{"type":"text","text":" change: where each item is, what is lit, the score, the turn count, which things have been touched, and your "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" values."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The entire mutable state is a single "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Every change funnels through it, so a turn commits atomically at its end (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") and save\/restore is a serialization call rather than a feature threaded through the codebase."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you write "},{"code":"cloak.isWorn","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"player.score += 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a rule, you are reading and writing that one state value through the entity’s token — never touching the definition, and never seeing another turn’s half-finished changes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"See also","anchor":"See-also","type":"heading","level":2},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a single Swift type becomes a world the engine can run."}],"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Global":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Global","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Global","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","abstract":[{"text":"Custom game state with the same ergonomics as built-in state:","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Global","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/global"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WorldMapAndExits":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMapAndExits","abstract":[{"text":"How rooms connect, and where everything starts.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/worldmapandexits","title":"The World Map and Its Exits"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Game":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Game"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A complete game: declarations, geography, and rules.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Game"}],"title":"Game","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/game","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/ContentBundles":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","abstract":[{"text":"Give a region its own declarations — its own type, and even its own package.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/contentbundles","title":"Content Bundles"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/adjectives(_:)":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"adjectives","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"...) -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9ItemTraitV","text":"ItemTrait","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"adjectives(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Additional words the parser accepts before the item’s noun.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameWorld/init(game:saveDirectory:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld\/init(game:saveDirectory:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"convenience"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"game"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4GameP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Game"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"saveDirectory"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation3URLV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"URL"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Builds the world from a game definition, validating it up front."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The random stream is seeded fresh each run; use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(game:seed:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to replay a specific one."}],"title":"init(game:saveDirectory:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gameworld\/init(game:savedirectory:)","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Item"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A thing in the world."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Item","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameContent":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GameContent","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GameContent","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A self-contained slice of a game’s world: its own rooms, items, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" state, plus the geography, rules, and verbs that go with them."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gamecontent","title":"GameContent"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WorldMap":{"title":"WorldMap","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WorldMap","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WorldMap","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap","abstract":[{"text":"The geography and initial placements of a game, declared in one block:","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/worldmap","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/scenery(_:adjectives:synonyms:description:_:)":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/scenery(_:adjectives:synonyms:description:_:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ",